HST Office: Scripting.Dictionary in VBA code, on every platform (owner request for 1.0.0-beta.5).

CreateObject("Scripting.Dictionary") needed the Windows scripting runtime through COM and failed
everywhere else ("Module cannot be loaded"). basic now has its own Dictionary object
(basic/source/classes/sbxdictionary.cxx, created by SbiFactory for "Scripting.Dictionary" and
"Dictionary", so CreateObject, New Scripting.Dictionary and New Dictionary all work):
- Add (error 457 on a duplicate key), Item (get and let), d(key) / d(key) = value (the default
  member is the stored item itself; a missing key is added, as in VBA), Exists, Remove (error 32811
  when missing), RemoveAll, Count, Keys / Items (0-based arrays), CompareMode (vbBinaryCompare,
  vbTextCompare: case-insensitive keys, also for Vietnamese letters).
- For Each k In d iterates over the keys (runtime.cxx).
- Keys may be strings, numbers or objects; items keep their type (nested dictionaries work).

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); the new
basic/source/classes/sbxdictionary.cxx is MPL-2.0 like its neighbours.
Test: tests/runtime/check-vba.py (calc-dictionary*, writer-dictionary* cases).
